# 20. OFFLINE-FIRST FUNCTIONALITY

The application must work without internet access.

Use Drift/SQLite as the primary local data store.

All core operations must work offline:

- Creating transactions.
- Editing transactions.
- Managing accounts.
- Viewing balances.
- Viewing analytics.
- Managing budgets.
- Tracking savings.
- Recording repayments.

Design cloud synchronization using a repository and synchronization service abstraction.

When Supabase is configured:

- Synchronize records securely.
- Track synchronization status.
- Handle pending changes.
- Handle failed synchronization.
- Avoid duplicate records.
- Use stable UUIDs.
- Handle conflicting updates explicitly.
- Provide manual retry.

Never overwrite newer financial data silently.

Local data must remain available if cloud connectivity is unavailable.

